#reason test/lantern-bundle.test.ts The description-wording test is dropped; the length cap on descriptions stays as its own test.
#reason test/lantern-code-reviewer.test.ts The two prose tests on the reviewer skill and agent are dropped; the list tests stay.
#reason test/lantern-delegate-complex.test.ts Prose about heavy tasks and the mapper is dropped; model kinds, policy and transcript lint stay.
#reason test/lantern-delegate-delivery.test.ts Protocol sentence tests go; the delivery values still match the bullets.
#reason test/lantern-delegate-required-skills.test.ts Protocol and agent wording tests go; the lists and the names-none guards stay.
#reason test/lantern-delegate-skill.test.ts Wording of SKILL.md and protocol.md is not behaviour; structure and the command lint stay.
#reason test/lantern-headless-permissions.test.ts Wording assertions on SKILL.md and mapper.md go; command coverage stays.
#reason test/lantern-plan-skills.test.ts Line-count and trigger-phrase checks on skill text go; the registry checks stay.
#reason test/lantern-sync-selftest.test.ts The exact floor sentence is pinned elsewhere and is only wording here.
#reason test/lantern-delegate-pick-conventions.test.ts Every test was a regex on skill and reviewer wording, so the file goes.
#story Developers stop maintaining wording tests
#step actor A developer
#step action rewords a skill or protocol text
#step subject the test suite
#file test/lantern-delegate-skill.test.ts
#file test/lantern-delegate-delivery.test.ts
#below interaction Rewords skills without touching tests
#below consequence A reworded sentence turned the suite red => Only structural breakage fails the suite
